      children: "GATE 2024 Computer Science paper was notable for a shift toward conceptual depth rather than rote memorization. The paper had 65 questions (10 GA + 55 Technical), carrying a total of 100 marks. The Technical section was divided across 8 core subjects with increased emphasis on Computer Networks and DBMS. The number of Numerical Answer Type (NAT) questions increased to 18, up from 15 in 2023, reflecting the examiners' preference for precise computation. Approximately 8 MSQs tested multi-correct understanding. The GA section included a new passage-based comprehension question that required inferential reading, breaking from previous direct-question patterns."
